  {
    "id": "crown_stand",
    "name": "The empty stand",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "A cushion of red velvet on a plinth of white stone. The dent where the Crown sat is still there.",
      "Someone has swept the stairs, but a little black ash is caught in the grain of the step."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "notice_board",
    "name": "Notice board",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WANTED: strong backs to fell pine for the gate. Ask Hob at the south gate.",
      "LOST: one brown mare. Do not ask Tam where. He knows.",
      "The Warden asks that no one go into the Crown Tower after dark. No reason is given.",
      "Smiths pay good bits for bronze bars. Copper and tin lie in the Old Quarry, east of the wall."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_north",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "North road: the Mossgate Reach ends at the treeline. Nothing past it has been charted. South: Caer Aldmoor, one hour."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_south",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "South road. West: Rabbit Meadow and the trapper's cabin. East: Mere Pool and the angler's dock. Straight on: the Tumbledown Watch."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_west",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "West road. The Whispering Pines and the woodcutter's lodge lie ahead. The Goblin Warren is north of the pines. Go with food."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_east",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "East road. The bridge over Silverrun Creek is just ahead. Beyond it: the Old Quarry and Hollow Farm."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_warren",
    "name": "Warning sign",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "GOBLIN WARREN. Pinegrubs and nutcrackers inside, and something larger at the back. Once the big one has you, you cannot run. Four people went in this season and three came back."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_pond",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Mere Pool. Shrimp in the shallows. The dock is for anglers; the lamp is Marl's and he will know if you move it."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_quarry",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Old Quarry. Copper and tin for any back strong enough. Dunstan buys ore at fair weight."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_farm",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Hollow Farm. Follow the lane south. Shut the field gate behind you."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_ruins",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Tumbledown Watch. A guard post from before the walls. It fell down before anyone now living was born. Mind the stones."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ruin_stone",
    "name": "Carved stone",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "A worn block in the middle of the ruin, with a ring of letters round the edge. The weather has taken most of them.",
      "What is left reads: HERE THE WATCH KEPT THE ROAD. Someone has scratched underneath it: and then it did not."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "dunhollow_board",
    "name": "Notice board",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WANTED: hands for the Drainage Cut. Marrow pays in iron bits. Bring birch logs and iron ore to the office.",
      "REWARD: any word of the second shift. Six went down the Delve and did not come up. Ask Corley at the mouth.",
      "Sump rats in the ore store again. Peg will pay a bounty. She does not say how much.",
      "Smith wants iron bars. Smelt them at the furnace. Smithing level 10."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "signal_stone",
    "name": "Signal beacon stone",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "A blackened stone basin on the floor of the ruined tower, where the signal fire burned. It has not burned for a long time.",
      "A rope has been tied to the rim and run out through the gap in the wall, toward the Delve. The knot is a miner's knot."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_downs_north",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "South road to Dunhollow. The Downs are open ground: sump rats, cave bats, and boars that do not wait to be asked. The old signal tower is east, off the road."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_dunhollow",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Dunhollow, one furlong. A mining village. The inn has beds, the office has work, and the smith will buy your bars."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_rocks",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "Ironback Rocks. Iron for a level 10 pick, coal for a better one. Keep your back to the wall when the boars come down from the hill."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_delve",
    "name": "Warning sign",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "DELVE OF THE BLACK SUMP. Flooded workings. Do not go in alone. Rats in the first galleries, bats in the east cave, wretches in the pools. At the bottom, the Foreman. You cannot run from him."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "town_well",
    "name": "Old well",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "The water is cold and hums a little at night. Everyone in Caer Aldmoor has stopped noticing."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "innsharrow_board",
    "name": "Trade board",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WANTED: strong lines and steady hands at the piers. The harbormaster pays for trout, a lot of trout.",
      "NO QUESTIONS ASKED, NO QUESTIONS ANSWERED. Inquire at the Gull's Rest. (Someone has crossed this out. Someone else has written it again.)",
      "The best trade board in the realm, they say. Look closely at the cargo lists. The weights never add up."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_coast_north",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "COAST ROAD. West along the cut, then south to Innsharrow. Far. Take food."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_innsharrow",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "INNSHARROW. Port city. Tavern, quay, piers. Dunes to the east, marsh to the west. Keep to the road after dark."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_innsharrow_west",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "MARSH. Wretches in the shallows. Not a place to walk with a full pack."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_innsharrow_east",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "THE DUNES. Boars root in the sand. They hit harder than they look."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "wargwatch_board",
    "name": "Hunters' board",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WANTED: wolves, dead. Pelts paid by the Warden. Heads not wanted.",
      "FOR SALE: one very good bow, one careful owner. Inquire at the Bowyer.",
      "WARNING: do not feed the pack. Do not feed anything. (Someone has written \"too late\" under this.)"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_moor_causeway",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "MARSH CAUSEWAY. South shore road to Wargwatch. Keep to the planks. The tide comes in quickly."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_wargwatch",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WARGWATCH. Hunters' lodge, trapper, bowyer, smokehouse. The mounds are not for climbing."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_cairns",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "THE NAMELESS CAIRNS. Nobody carved the names. Do not carve yours."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "naerwick_board",
    "name": "Village board",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "WANTED: steady hands for the lamps. Bring your own oil.",
      "NOTICE: coins in your net belong to the lake. Return them. (Someone has written \"they do not want them back\".)",
      "LOST: one boat, one dog. The dog came back."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_naerwick",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "NAERWICK. Stilt village on Lake Aelmere. Walk the planks. Lanterns burn all night."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_drowned_hall",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "THE DROWNED HALL. No one built it. No one has come back to say who did."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sign_lake_road",
    "name": "Signpost",
    "kind": "inspect",
    "text": [
      "LAKE ROAD. South along the shore, then east to Naerwick. The marsh is not safe after dark."
    ]
  }
]
